      "solution": ["The left mini-grid turns clockwise by 90°, then 180°, then 270°, then 360° (a full turn), then 90° again; the turn increases by 90° each time modulo a full turn. Frames 1–6, left mini-grid: [white, black, white, white] in reading order → [white, white, white, black] in reading order → [black, white, white, white] in reading order → [white, white, black, white] in reading order → [white, white, black, white] in reading order → [black, white, white, white] in reading order. Next: [white, white, white, black] in reading order.","the middle mini-grid turns 90° anticlockwise each frame. Frames 1–6, middle mini-grid: [black, black, white, white] in reading order → [black, white, black, white] in reading order → [white, white, black, black] in reading order → [white, black, white, black] in reading order → [black, black, white, white] in reading order → [black, white, black, white] in reading order. Next: [white, white, black, black] in reading order.","rotate the left grid clockwise by the bottom arrow's angle measured clockwise from up in THAT frame, then union it with the middle grid to obtain the right grid. Frames 1–6, right mini-grid: [black, black, black, white] in reading order → [black, black, black, white] in reading order → [black, white, black, black] in reading order → [black, black, white, black] in reading order → [black, black, white, white] in reading order → [black, white, black, white] in reading order. Next: [white, white, black, black] in reading order. A corresponding cell is black when at least one input is black, including when both are black.","the bottom arrow turns 90° clockwise each frame. Frames 1–6, bottom arrow: 180° clockwise from up → 270° clockwise from up → 0° clockwise from up → 90° clockwise from up → 180° clockwise from up → 270° clockwise from up. Next: 0° clockwise from up."],
