      "hints": ["Compare each frame with the one before it: which single row or column of the grid has moved?","Do the moves alternate between a row and a column? Then check the background and the corner marker separately.","Predict the grid, background and marker before looking at the options."],
      "solution": ["Grid: the moves alternate. From frame 1 to 2 the middle row moves one cell to the right; from frame 2 to 3 the left column moves one cell down; the pattern repeats, wrapping round. Next (frame 5 to 6): the middle row moves one cell to the right.","Background: grey → white → grey → white → grey. It alternates, so next: white.","Corner marker: top-right → bottom-right → bottom-left → top-left → top-right, one corner clockwise each step. Next: bottom-right.","Marker colour: black → white → black → white → black. Next: white."],
      "explanation": "Four independent rules apply: the grid alternates between two shifts (the middle row moves one cell to the right, then the left column moves one cell down); the background alternates; the corner marker moves one corner clockwise; the marker colour alternates. Work out each rule from consecutive frames, predict the next frame, then eliminate. Option similarity alone is not evidence of a rule.",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "optionNotes": ["Wrong: the grid uses a shift of column 3 up instead of the next alternating move.","Wrong: the corner marker is at the wrong corner.","Wrong: the grid repeats the last frame instead of making the next alternating move; the marker has the wrong fill.","Wrong: the grid uses a shift of row 3 left instead of the next alternating move; the corner marker is at the wrong corner.","Correct: the middle row moves one cell to the right; background white; marker bottom-right, white."],
