      "hints": ["Track each mini-grid separately. Then compare corresponding cells across the three grids within a frame; also follow the bottom arrow.","Compare matching cells within each frame. Does black mean either input is black, or exactly one? Check whether the bottom arrow controls a preliminary turn.","The left mini-grid turns anticlockwise by 90°, then 180°, then 270°, then 360° (a full turn), then 90° again; the turn increases by 90° each time modulo a full turn. the middle mini-grid turns 90° clockwise each frame. Predict the remaining colour/count or panel features before choosing."],
      "optionNotes": ["Correct: left mini-grid: [black, white, white, white] in reading order; middle mini-grid: [white, white, black, black] in reading order; right mini-grid: [white, white, black, black] in reading order; bottom arrow: 180° clockwise from up.","Wrong: right mini-grid is [black, black, white, white] in reading order; it should be [white, white, black, black] in reading order; bottom arrow is 0° clockwise from up; it should be 180° clockwise from up.","Wrong: left mini-grid is [white, white, black, white] in reading order; it should be [black, white, white, white] in reading order; right mini-grid is [black, black, white, white] in reading order; it should be [white, white, black, black] in reading order.","Wrong: left mini-grid is [black, black, black, white] in reading order; it should be [black, white, white, white] in reading order; middle mini-grid is [white, white, white, white] in reading order; it should be [white, white, black, black] in reading order.","Wrong: right mini-grid is [white, black, white, black] in reading order; it should be [white, white, black, black] in reading order."],
      "solution": ["The left mini-grid turns anticlockwise by 90°, then 180°, then 270°, then 360° (a full turn), then 90° again; the turn increases by 90° each time modulo a full turn. Frames 1–6, left mini-grid: [white, black, white, white] in reading order → [black, white, white, white] in reading order → [white, white, white, black] in reading order → [white, white, black, white] in reading order → [white, white, black, white] in reading order → [white, white, white, black] in reading order. Next: [black, white, white, white] in reading order.","the middle mini-grid turns 90° clockwise each frame. Frames 1–6, middle mini-grid: [black, black, white, white] in reading order → [white, black, white, black] in reading order → [white, white, black, black] in reading order → [black, white, black, white] in reading order → [black, black, white, white] in reading order → [white, black, white, black] in reading order. Next: [white, white, black, black] in reading order.","in each frame first turn the left grid 90° anticlockwise, then combine its black cells with those of the middle grid: a cell in the right grid is black if either input is black. Frames 1–6, right mini-grid: [black, black, white, white] in reading order → [white, black, black, black] in reading order → [white, black, black, black] in reading order → [black, white, black, black] in reading order → [black, black, white, black] in reading order → [white, black, white, black] in reading order. Next: [white, white, black, black] in reading order. A corresponding cell is black when at least one input is black, including when both are black.","the bottom arrow turns 90° anticlockwise each frame. Frames 1–6, bottom arrow: 0° clockwise from up → 270° clockwise from up → 180° clockwise from up → 90° clockwise from up → 0° clockwise from up → 270° clockwise from up. Next: 180° clockwise from up."],
